      "anchor": "Fired at session start and not in flight. Reading the two governing specs before designing caught three wrong premises: #626 claiming zero production callers when the mechanics exist and only the wiring is missing, #626 asking for an automatic archive its own Eighth Slice supersedes, and the handoff asking for a score no declared session can carry. It then failed to transfer to in-flight assertions: the catalog gate was spelled `python3 scripts/...` on the belief that run_when gates availability when _catalog_gate_path only recognizes ./ commands, and \"exits zero always\" was written without reading the entrypoint wrapper. Reviewers caught both."
